      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "German settlers arrived around 1721 and Acadian exiles followed in 1755, turning Darrow into a multicultural colonial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/darrow_louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Darrow hosts antebellum plantations like Houmas House and Hermitage Museum, showcasing early 19th‑century Greek Revival sugarcane estates.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/darrow_louisiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The low‑lying alluvial plain makes Darrow prone to frequent flooding from the Mississippi and its tributaries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/darrow_louisiana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Beneath Darrow lies the Darrow salt dome, a subsurface structure that shapes local hydrology and stability.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/darrow_louisiana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Darrow enjoys a humid subtropical climate with hot summers, mild winters, and over 60 inches of annual rainfall.",
